  "native_method": "Fresh database per suite, original service methods and ordinary role/scope checks; pg_blocking_pids and NOWAIT/advisory locks verify actual wait order. Only notification delivery is suppressed.",
  "verified": [
    "Claim review locks its signature before any competing claim request, including direct claim and claim creation.",
    "Competing claim approvals cannot both transfer ownership; losing requests become canceled and a later approval returns 409.",
    "Direct same-name claim cancels old pending claims and keeps teacher/student IDs distinct.",
    "New claim creation waiting for a transfer reloads the current owner and reviewer.",
    "Reverse batch order locks signatures consistently before requests.",
    "Legacy requests with no snapshot acquire their known material lock before flow/request/reviewer writes.",
    "Manual binding waits for the material before its binding advisory lock.",
    "Assessment-plan revision rotation waits for the plan before canceling child decisions.",
    "Request signature association changes while waiting are rejected after locks are acquired.",
    "Ordinary approve/cancel/end races retain the winning state and cannot overwrite applied flows."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "This is not full signature-domain concurrency certification or production load testing.",
    "Account identity propagation and signature edit/create/merge still require a shared cross-domain lock protocol; those operations were not made available to the Agent by this change.",
    "Claim operations are not enabled in the Agent capability catalog despite these local normal-Web fixes.",
    "The HTTP document-request tests replace document artifact rendering with synthetic artifacts; signature consumption/rendered production documents are outside this evidence.",
    "The material binding proof uses an empty replacement to isolate real lock order; it does not claim a new signature-application feature."
  ],
